  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 121 AM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nMonday through Saturday:\n\nHigh pressure builds in Monday and lingers through Tuesday, with\nlight winds and highs in the upper 70s to low 80s. Low pressure\ndevelops in the Plains Tuesday, phasing with a shortwave moving\nthrough northern portions of the Upper Midwest. This will lead to\nchances for thunderstorms late Tuesday night into Wednesday\n(20-40%). Timing of these storms will determine impacts, with \nless instability to work with if storms develop during the \novernight hours. Bulk shear values remain quite weak (10-20 kt)\nthrough Wednesday, with low pressure ejecting eastward into\nWednesday night and bringing higher shear values (40-50 kt)\nWednesday night into Thursday. This will lead to better chances\nfor severe weather, but timing and upper ridging may prevent\nthunderstorms from impacting southern Wisconsin directly. Model\nuncertainty leads to PoPs of 15-25% through this period. Thursday\ninto Friday, low pressure propagates eastward, with high pressure\nbuilding back in from Canada, allowing for drier conditions and\nincreasing temperatures (mid to upper 80s) into next weekend.\n\nMH",
